@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.36.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.36.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.36.0 (2026-11-24): The repeated stories of chapter 10 are replaced and Windows is the default platform of chapters 10 and 11. Both stories are done."""@en .

ex:TK11_Repeats_10_Build backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Files: story companion 08-tooling/sen0414_ch10_stories_v1_1_0.py (the UTF-8 and JSON stories replaced by a 1983 MS-DOS backslash story and a 1974 CP/M drive letter story), deck 4.4.0 (41 slides, as before), page 9.23.0; pictures are two public-domain MS-DOS screens from Wikimedia Commons (no photographs of people were added); links to Larry Osterman's Microsoft post and the Wikipedia article on drive letters." .
ex:TK11_Repeats_10_Verify backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Story repeat check over chapters 1 to 25: no repeat of a chapter 10 story (the dbm story only shares a person's name with chapters 8 and 9, a different event). Deck checks clean (standard 13 of 13, fit, layout, notes, overlap, reader notes, story prose); code check 0 findings; page test 9.23.0: 406 passed, 0 failed, widgets 59 of 59. Still open: the older Ken Thompson photograph is kept on the dbm slide as it was." .
ex:ST11_Repeats_10 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Criterion met for chapter 10: no story repeats another chapter's story, slide count 41, checks and page test pass." .
ex:TK11_Windows_Build backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Files: 08-tooling/sen0414_windows_setup_v1_1_0.json (the hidden set-up lines), sources 1.3.0 (chapter 10) and 1.4.0 (chapter 11), decks 4.4.0 and 4.3.0, manifests 1.6.0, A-boxes 1.0.3, pages 9.23.0 and 9.24.0, question bank 1.1.0 (two programs now use os.fspath). Measured on the way: set-up 1.0.0 broke folder listing on absolute paths (13 panels had no set-up entry and the string form was used by pathlib itself); 1.1.0 shows the Windows form only to the program's own code." .
ex:TK11_Windows_Verify backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Deck checks clean for both decks; code check 0 findings (18 and 19 examples); page tests 9.23.0 (406 passed, 0 failed) and 9.24.0 (410 passed, 0 failed), widgets 59 of 59 and 64 of 64. Known limit, stated: a learner who turns a path into text with str() and uses it as a file name on an absolute path will find it does not open in the browser, where it would on a real Windows computer; os.fspath gives the working form. The older question bank checker needs Python 3.14, which this machine does not have, so it was not run on bank 1.1.0; the page test re-ran all 42 coded questions instead. The prediction field of the page is still one line; results themselves may span lines." .
ex:ST11_Windows backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Criterion met: Windows paths show in every example, result and Try it of both chapters, multi-line results are accepted and shown, and the tests pass. Not part of the criterion and left open as a recommendation: a multi-line prediction field in the page template." .
